;; The one-shot fiber fallback must report, not abort().
;;
;; A handle whose body reaches its `perform` through a form the driver cannot
;; descend -- here a `catch-unwind` thunk -- is rejected by ws_capturable and
;; runs on a ucontext fiber instead of the work-stack.  That fiber is
;; single-shot: once the body finishes there is nothing to re-enter, and a
;; second resume used to swapcontext into the dead fiber and land on
;; eval_body_thunk's abort() -- the interpreter dying with no message, which at
;; a REPL takes the session with it.
;;
;; requires.interp-only: this is an interpreter-path diagnostic, owned by
;; tests/run-turi.sh (which runs it under `--interpret`); the compiled suite
;; PASS-skips it.  The compiled path rejects the same program for its own
;; unrelated reason -- a perform inside a catch-unwind thunk is outside the CPS
;; backend's subset -- so asserting this text there would assert the wrong
;; mechanism.
;;
;; If the driver ever learns to descend catch-unwind thunks, pick a different
;; non-capturable shape rather than deleting the assertion -- the fallback
;; still exists and must still report.
(defeffect Ask [] : int)

(defn main [] : int
  (println (handle (ok-val (catch-unwind (fn [] : int (perform (Ask)))))
                   (Ask [] ^multishot k) (+ (resume k 1) (resume k 2))))
  0)
